# Release archives (`git archive`, the GitHub tarball) leave these out. They stay
# in the tree and in history; only the shipped archive drops them.
# CLAUDE.md is agent context for this checkout, not for a plugin user.
# .claude-plugin/ sits at the repo root, so this is also the plugin root, and
# `claude plugin validate --strict` fails on a CLAUDE.md there.
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
# design/ holds the maintainers' internal notes: rulings, crew process, task
# IDs, and a quote from a private chat. It stays in the tree and in history
# for whoever works on sessionphone; shipped docs state their rules inline
# instead of pointing into it. Both lines are needed: `/design/` drops the
# directory (without it the archive keeps an empty `design/` entry), and
# `/design/**` marks each file, which `git check-attr` reports per path.
/design/ export-ignore
/design/** export-ignore
